WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.630
They told me politics was the art of the possible.

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:09.640
I was twenty-six, on a borrowed stage in a small town square — and nothing seemed impossible.

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.060
I learned to govern a city first. Its streets, its budgets, its patience.

4
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.250
Then the party. Every vote, a negotiation. Every ally, a future rival.

5
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.100
The seventies tested everything we believed.

6
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:37.020
Strikes in the factories. Fear in the streets. Decisions taken at three in the morning.

7
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.110
Then television changed the rules.

8
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.830
A single sentence could win an election — or end a career.

9
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.910
Ministries. Coalitions. The long corridors of power.

10
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.220
And I lost. Years in opposition taught me more than any victory.

11
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.640
Until one night, the count turned our way.

12
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.310
I led a nation through crises I never saw coming.

13
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.750
Some, I solved. Some, I survived.

14
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.680
Now it is your turn. Any nation.

15
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:35.240
Any decade. The years will test you, your allies will doubt you, your rivals will wait.

16
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:40.870
Few reach the end of their mandate with their name intact. Will you?
